A new version of the "treasure island" patch, with the following
modifications:

1. Some unusued variables and awkwardnesses in the island code have
been removed.  Overall, islands themselves are unchanged in this
version.
2. Islands now produce sound messages when they're on your current
level, adapted from suggestions from the group.
3. The code that decides what room will appear on a random level has
been restructured a little.  Before, only one special room could
appear on a level (not including vaults, which were handled
separately).  Now rooms have been divided into three categories,
Shops, Zoos (monster rooms) and Terrain (temples and islands), and up
to one of each may appear at roughly the same probability as before. 
Note that although it's possible to get a Shop/Zoo/Terrain level, in
practice it doesn't happen often.  (I've never seen it occur in my
tests.)
4. Swamps have been moved out of the room decision part of mklev,
since they aren't really a "room" type at all.  Since swamps now get
first crack at being generated when the level is deep enough, they
seem to be a little more common now.  A swamp level forbids the other
special rooms from being made.
5. There's now a new kind of similar level modification, an
underground river that appears on about one-in-seven levels, in the
grand D&D river-through-the-dungeon tradition.  It can either flow
horizontally or vertically through the map, cutting through the stone
as if by erosion.  It doesn't block movement like the island does;
places where there would ordinarily get stone or wall where the river
flows mostly get water instead, corridors and both kinds of door
become normal floor, and anything else is unchanged.  Shops are an
exception; they do not lose their walls because of the river, which
would make it too easy to steal.  The water doesn't block
line-of-sight (imagine a long, airy chamber with water flowing a few
feet deep), so you can see some of the level before you actually get
there.

Bugs:
1. The lava island and the river, if they should happen to be in the
same place, may be problematic.  At the very least it might look
weird.
2. I couldn't figure out how to check if a vault is in the river. 
They really should keep their walls.  Sometimes this produces awkward
behavior when guards show up to lead the player out of the vault,
including fake doorways getting produced and kelp getting stuck in
suddenly-occuring vault wallification.  Surprisingly, the guard is
still perfectly able to lead the player back to the "main" level. 
Does anyone know a way to fix this?  Neither Source searches nor
testing have yet come up with an easy solution.
3. So far, the river doesn't have appropriate monsters.

The diff (about 15k) is at:
http://www.hiddenglade.com/download/island1-1.diff

This expects to be applied to a virgin Nethack source tree; it's not
an incremental patch.  Sorry about that, I'm still getting used to
